          "title": "You'll want to know: महात्मा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "महात्मा — mahātmā — \"a great soul; a noble person\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "महात्मा दरिद्रस्य साहाय्यं करोति। mahātmā daridrasya sāhāyyaṃ karoti. A noble soul helps the poor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "महात्मा (mahātmā) is built from महत्, \"great\", and आत्मा, \"the self, the soul\"; MW gives \"high-souled, magnanimous, noble\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
